\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h That's better.

400
00:28:13.060 --> 00:28:14.360
  You've been very helpful.

401
00:28:14.430 --> 00:28:15.930
   No stop please!

402
00:28:15.990 --> 00:28:18.300
  What are you doing?
  Please stop!\h\h\h\h\h\h

403
00:28:18.360 --> 00:28:20.930
  Please stop! No! No!

404
00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:23.200
I told you everything! No!

405
00:28:23.270 --> 00:28:25.170
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hNo! (SCREAMING)
\h
   (RAT CLATTERING)\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

406
00:28:27.340 --> 00:28:28.570
   ARYA: Joffrey.

407
00:28:30.140 --> 00:28:31.340
Cersei.

408
00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:34.510
 Ilyn Payne. The Hound.

409
00:28:34.580 --> 00:28:37.010
   WOMAN: Please Polliver.
   Some food.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

410
00:28:37.750 --> 00:28:39.550
 Just a crust of bread.

411
00:28:41.820 --> 00:28:43.190
 (WOMAN CRYING)

412
00:28:43.990 --> 00:28:45.250
   Polliver.

413
00:28:46.160 --> 00:28:47.620
 The Mountain.

414
00:29:05.610 --> 00:29:08.540
 STANNIS:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 Lady Stark I had not thought\h
 to find you in the Stormlands.

415
00:29:08.610 --> 00:29:11.510
 I had not thought to\h\h
 be here Lord Stannis.

416
00:29:12.450 --> 00:29:13.680
 Can that truly be you?

417
00:29:13.750 --> 00:29:15.690
 Who else might it be?

418
00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:18.720
  When I saw your standard
  I couldn't be sure.\h\h\h\h\h\h

419
00:29:18.790 --> 00:29:20.760
  Whose banner is that?
\h
\h\h\h\h My own.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

420
00:29:22.230 --> 00:29:23.530
 I suppose if we\h\h\h
 used the same one

421
00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:26.160
the battle would be
terribly confusing.

422
00:29:26.230 --> 00:29:28.330
  Why is your stag on fire?

423
00:29:29.470 --> 00:29:31.530
 The king has\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 taken for his sigil

424
00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:33.600
 the fiery heart of
 the Lord of Light.

425
00:29:33.670 --> 00:29:37.670
 Ah you must be\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 this fire priestess\h\h\h
 we hear so much about.

426
00:29:38.510 --> 00:29:40.580
  Mmm brother

427
00:29:40.650 --> 00:29:43.550
 now I understand\h\h\h\h\h\h
 why you found religion
 in your old age.\h\h\h\h\h\h

428
00:29:43.620 --> 00:29:44.980
 Watch yourself Renly.

429
00:29:45.050 --> 00:29:46.850
 RENLY: No no
 I'm relieved.\h

430
00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:50.250
I never really believed
you were a fanatic.\h\h\h\h

431
00:29:50.320 --> 00:29:53.220
  Charmless rigid
  a bore yes\h\h\h\h\h

432
00:29:53.290 --> 00:29:55.360
   but not a godly man.

433
00:29:55.430 --> 00:29:57.860
  You should kneel\h\h\h\h
  before your brother.

434
00:29:57.930 --> 00:30:00.330
He's the Lord's chosen

435
00:30:00.400 --> 00:30:02.470
  born amidst salt and smoke.

436
00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:05.270
Born amidst salt and smoke?

437
00:30:05.340 --> 00:30:07.900
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h   Is he a ham?
\h
 STANNIS: That's twice\h\h\h\h\h
 I've warned you.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

438
00:30:07.970 --> 00:30:09.940
 Listen to yourselves.

439
00:30:10.010 --> 00:30:12.710
 If you were sons of mine
 I would knock\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 your heads together\h\h\h\h\h\h

440
00:30:12.780 --> 00:30:16.450
 and lock you in a bedchamber
 until you remembered\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 that you were brothers.\h\h\h\h\h

441
00:30:16.510 --> 00:30:19.620
 It is strange to find you
 beside my brother\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 Lady Stark.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

442
00:30:19.680 --> 00:30:21.950
Your husband was\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
a supporter of my claim.

443
00:30:22.020 --> 00:30:24.520
  Lord Eddard's integrity
  cost him his head.\h\h\h\h\h

444
00:30:24.590 --> 00:30:27.060
  And you sit\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  beside this pretender
  and chastise me.\h\h\h\h\h

445
00:30:27.130 --> 00:30:28.860
   We share a common enemy.

446
00:30:28.930 --> 00:30:31.590
   The Iron Throne\h\h
   is mine by right.

447
00:30:32.760 --> 00:30:34.730
All those that\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
deny that are my foes.

448
00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:39.370
 The whole realm denies it
 from Dorne to the Wall.\h\h\h

449
00:30:39.440 --> 00:30:41.200
Old men deny it\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
with their death rattle

450
00:30:41.270 --> 00:30:43.640
and unborn children deny it
in their mother's wombs.\h\h\h

451
00:30:46.340 --> 00:30:48.580
   No one wants you
   for their king.\h

452
00:30:48.650 --> 00:30:51.180
  You never wanted\h\h\h\h\h
  any friends brother.

453
00:30:51.250 --> 00:30:53.550
  But a man without friends
  is a man without power.\h\h

454
00:30:54.850 --> 00:30:57.290
For the sake of\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
the mother who bore us

455
00:30:57.360 --> 00:31:00.720
   I will give you this\h\h\h\h
   one night to reconsider.

456
00:31:00.790 --> 00:31:04.990
   Strike your banners\h\h\h
   come to me before dawn

457
00:31:05.060 --> 00:31:08.260
 and I will grant you\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 your old seat in the Council.

458
00:31:09.270 --> 00:31:11.300
 I'll even name you my heir

459
00:31:12.440 --> 00:31:13.600
  until a son is born to me.

460
00:31:15.870 --> 00:31:17.940
 Otherwise I shall
 destroy you.\h\h\h\h\h

461
00:31:22.150 --> 00:31:23.680
  Look across those fields
  brother.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

462
00:31:24.950 --> 00:31:26.580
 Can you see\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 all those banners?

463
00:31:26.650 --> 00:31:29.090
 You think a few bolts of cloth
 will make you king?\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

464
00:31:29.150 --> 00:31:31.490
 RENLY: No.

465
00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:35.060
   The men holding\h\h\h\h\h
   those bolts of cloth
   will make me king.\h\h

466
00:31:35.130 --> 00:31:36.590
   We shall see Renly.

467
00:31:36.660 --> 00:31:39.260
 Come the dawn we shall see.

468
00:31:39.330 --> 00:31:41.500
  Look to your sins
  Lord Renly.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

469
00:31:41.570 --> 00:31:43.630
 The night is dark\h\h\h
 and full of terrors.

470
00:31:49.670 --> 00:31:52.640
Would you believe
I loved him once?

471
00:32:13.500 --> 00:32:15.700
 I thought we were welcome.

472
00:32:15.770 --> 00:32:18.200
  If you heard a Dothraki horde
  was approaching your city\h\h\h

473
00:32:18.270 --> 00:32:20.100
 you might do the same
 Khaleesi.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

474
00:32:22.670 --> 00:32:23.840
  Horde?

475
00:32:39.620 --> 00:32:41.660
 My name is Daenerys...

476
00:32:41.730 --> 00:32:45.230
Daenerys Stormborn of
the house Targaryen.\h

477
00:32:45.300 --> 00:32:46.760
  You know me my lord?

478
00:32:46.830 --> 00:32:49.300
Only by reputation
Khaleesi.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

479
00:32:49.370 --> 00:32:52.440
   And I'm no lord\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
   merely a humble merchant.

480
00:32:54.340 --> 00:32:56.970
They call you\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
the Mother of Dragons.

481
00:32:57.040 --> 00:32:59.140
And what should
I call you?\h\h\h\h

482
00:32:59.210 --> 00:33:00.410
 Oh my name is quite long

483
00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:03.280
 and quite impossible\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 for foreigners to pronounce.

484
00:33:03.350 --> 00:33:06.180
I am simply\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
a trader of spices.

485
00:33:06.950 --> 00:33:10.250
 But we are the Thirteen

486
00:33:10.320 --> 00:33:13.690
   charged with the governance
   and protection of Qarth\h\h\h

487
00:33:13.760 --> 00:33:16.830
   the greatest city\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
   that ever was or will be.

488
00:33:18.260 --> 00:33:21.760
 The beauty of\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 Quarth is legendary...
\h
\h\h\h\hQarth.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

489
00:33:24.640 --> 00:33:26.340
 Qarth.

490
00:33:26.400 --> 00:33:28.440
 Might we see the dragons?

491
00:33:33.980 --> 00:33:36.350
   My friend

492
00:33:37.620 --> 00:33:39.780
 we have traveled very far.

493
00:33:39.850 --> 00:33:42.150
 We have no food no water.

494
00:33:42.220 --> 00:33:44.690
  Once I see my people fed
  I would be honored...\h\h\h\h

495
00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:47.890
  Forgive me\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  Mother of Dragons

496
00:33:47.960 --> 00:33:51.890
 but no man alive has\h
 seen a living dragon.

497
00:33:51.960 --> 00:33:53.830
   Some of my more\h\h
   skeptical friends

498
00:33:53.900 --> 00:33:57.100
   refuse to believe
   your children\h\h\h\h

499
00:33:57.840 --> 00:33:59.370
  even exist.

500
00:33:59.440 --> 00:34:02.270
   All we ask is the chance
   to see for ourselves.\h\h\h

501
00:34:03.510 --> 00:34:04.640
   I am not a liar.

502
00:34:04.710 --> 00:34:06.880
  Oh I don't think you are.

503
00:34:06.940 --> 00:34:08.340
 But as I've\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 never met you before

504
00:34:08.410 --> 00:34:11.010
   my opinion on the matter
   is of limited value.\h\h\h\h

505
00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:15.920
 Where I come from

506
00:34:15.990 --> 00:34:20.990
 guests are\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 treated with respect\h\h\h\h\h
 not insulted at the gates.

507
00:34:21.060 --> 00:34:24.360
 Then perhaps you should\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 return to where you come from.

508
00:34:24.430 --> 00:34:26.060
   We wish you well.

509
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.900
What are you doing?

510
00:34:31.970 --> 00:34:34.170
You promised to receive me.

511
00:34:35.610 --> 00:34:37.040
  We have received you.

512
00:34:37.110 --> 00:34:39.980
   Here we are\h\h\h\h\h
   and here you are.

513
00:34:40.050 --> 00:34:43.680
   If you do not let us in
   all of us will die.\h\h\h\h\h

514
00:34:43.750 --> 00:34:46.550
 Which we shall
 deeply regret.

515
00:34:46.620 --> 00:34:49.590
   But Qarth did not become
   the greatest city\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
   that ever was or will be

516
00:34:49.650 --> 00:34:52.920
by letting Dothraki savages
through its gates.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

517
00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:02.430
 Khaleesi please be careful.

518
00:35:05.300 --> 00:35:06.340
   Thirteen!

519
00:35:08.110 --> 00:35:13.610
 When my dragons are grown
 we will take back\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 what was stolen from me\h\h\h

520
00:35:13.680 --> 00:35:15.850
   and destroy those\h\h\h
   who have wronged me.

521
00:35:15.910 --> 00:35:21.320
 We will lay waste to armies\h\h\h
 and burn cities to the ground.

522
00:35:21.390 --> 00:35:24.920
   Turn us away and we\h
   will burn you first.

523
00:35:26.420 --> 00:35:27.790
Ah.

524
00:35:27.860 --> 00:35:30.190
 You are a true Targaryen.

525
00:35:31.630 --> 00:35:33.260
  Only as you said
  a moment ago\h\h\h\h

526
00:35:33.330 --> 00:35:35.760
  if we don't let\h\h\h
  you into the city
  you will all die.\h

527
00:35:36.500 --> 00:35:37.570
  And so...

528
00:35:37.640 --> 00:35:40.040
 Retreating in fear
 from a little girl

529
00:35:40.110 --> 00:35:42.440
  is unbecoming of\h
  the greatest city

530
00:35:42.510 --> 00:35:44.140
  that ever was or will be.

531
00:35:44.210 --> 00:35:47.680
The discussion is over
Xaro Xhoan Daxos.\h\h\h\h\h\h

532
00:35:47.750 --> 00:35:49.580
  The Thirteen have spoken.

533
00:35:49.650 --> 00:35:51.710
 I am one of the Thirteen

534
00:35:52.550 --> 00:35:55.050
 and I am still speaking.

535
00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:57.250
   The girl threatens
   to burn our city\h\h
   to the ground\h\h\h\h\h

536
00:35:57.320 --> 00:36:00.260
and you would invite her in
for a cup of wine?\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

537
00:36:00.330 --> 00:36:02.930
 She is\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 the Mother of Dragons.

538
00:36:02.990 --> 00:36:08.230
 Do you expect her to\h\h\h
 watch her people starve
 without breathing fire?

539
00:36:08.300 --> 00:36:10.730
 I believe we can\h\h\h\h
 allow a few Dothraki

540
00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:13.370
 through our gates\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 without dooming our city.

541
00:36:13.440 --> 00:36:16.510
 After all here I am

542
00:36:16.570 --> 00:36:20.440
  a savage from\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  the Summer Isles\h\h\h\h\h\h
  and Qarth still stands.

543
00:36:21.150 --> 00:36:23.010
 Our decision is final.

544
00:36:23.950 --> 00:36:25.280
   Very well.

545
00:36:28.250 --> 00:36:29.850
 I invoke soumai.

546
00:36:34.730 --> 00:36:37.330
 I will vouch for her
 her people\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

547
00:36:37.400 --> 00:36:39.930
 and her dragons\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 in accordance with the law.

548
00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:48.310
Be it on your head.

549
00:36:50.310 --> 00:36:52.470
 Welcome to Qarth
 my lady.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

550
00:37:42.360 --> 00:37:43.430
 MOUNTAIN: You.

551
00:37:53.440 --> 00:37:55.670
 TICKLER:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 Is there gold or silver
 in the village?\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

552
00:37:55.740 --> 00:37:57.410
  I'm not from the village.

553
00:37:57.480 --> 00:37:59.780
 Where is the Brotherhood?

554
00:37:59.840 --> 00:38:00.910
  I don't know\h
  what that is.

555
00:38:07.820 --> 00:38:09.050
  (SQUEAKING)

556
00:38:15.030 --> 00:38:16.460
  (HORSES NEIGH)

557
00:38:30.340 --> 00:38:34.380
 MAN: You two.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 Take Lord Lannister's\h\h
 things to his quarters.

558
00:38:34.910 --> 00:38:36.280
 What's this?

559
00:38:36.350 --> 00:38:40.150
We weren't expecting you\h\h
till tomorrow Lord Tywin.

560
00:38:40.220 --> 00:38:41.720
  (CHUCKLES) Evidently not.

561
00:38:43.950 --> 00:38:45.520
Why are\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
these prisoners not
in their cells?\h\h\h\h

562
00:38:45.590 --> 00:38:48.260
 MOUNTAIN: Cells are\h\h
 overflowing my lord.

563
00:38:48.330 --> 00:38:52.190
 POLLIVER:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 This lot won't be here long.\h\h
 Don't need no permanent place.

564
00:38:52.260 --> 00:38:55.560
 After we interrogate 'em
 we usually just...\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

565
00:38:55.630 --> 00:38:59.840
  Are we so well-manned\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  that we can afford to discard

566
00:38:59.900 --> 00:39:02.010
   able young bodies\h\h\h\h
   and skilled laborers?

567
00:39:11.980 --> 00:39:14.280
   You do you have a trade?

568
00:39:15.950 --> 00:39:17.090
 GENDRY: Smith my lord.

569
00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:20.920
   What are you looking at?
   Kneel!\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

570
00:39:22.830 --> 00:39:26.200
   Kneel or I'll carve\h
   your lungs out boy.

571
00:39:26.260 --> 00:39:28.160
 He'll do no such thing.

572
00:39:29.070 --> 00:39:31.500
This one's a girl
you idiot\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

573
00:39:32.440 --> 00:39:34.170
 dressed as a boy.

574
00:39:34.240 --> 00:39:36.470
  Why?\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h
   Safer to travel
   my lord.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

575
00:39:37.380 --> 00:39:39.140
   Smart.

576
00:39:39.210 --> 00:39:41.110
 More than I can\h\h
 say for this lot.

577
00:39:41.180 --> 00:39:43.850
   Get these prisoners to work.

578
00:39:43.910 --> 00:39:44.950
 Bring the girl.

579
00:39:46.020 --> 00:39:47.680
I need a new cupbearer.

580
00:39:47.750 --> 00:39:49.120
 MOUNTAIN: My lord.

581
00:39:49.190 --> 00:39:50.520
  (KNOCKING ON DOOR)

582
00:39:56.830 --> 00:39:58.730
 Your visits are\h
 too few cousin.

583
00:39:58.800 --> 00:40:00.100
  Her Grace\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  the Queen Regent

584
00:40:00.170 --> 00:40:02.830
commands you to release
Grand Maester Pycelle.\h

585
00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:03.930
   Here's your warrant.

586
00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:05.000
So it is.

587
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:08.370
 Will you take a cup with me?

588
00:40:08.440 --> 00:40:11.210
I find that mulled\h\h
wine helps me sleep.

589
00:40:11.280 --> 00:40:15.440
I am here at\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
Her Grace's behest\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
not to drink with you Imp.

590
00:40:15.510 --> 00:40:18.350
 If my sister was so\h\h\h
 concerned for Pycelle

591
00:40:18.420 --> 00:40:20.420
   I would have thought
   she'd come herself.\h

592
00:40:20.480 --> 00:40:23.620
 Instead she sends you.\h\h\h\h
 What am I to make of that?

593
00:40:23.690 --> 00:40:25.450
   I don't care\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
   what you make of it

594
00:40:25.520 --> 00:40:28.190
 so long as you release\h\h\h\h
 your prisoner immediately.

595
00:40:28.260 --> 00:40:32.390
  And you've received\h\h
  these instructions\h\h\h
  directly from Cersei?

596
00:40:32.460 --> 00:40:34.330
 As I said several times.

597
00:40:34.400 --> 00:40:37.930
And you've waited this long
to deliver the information?

598
00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:40.600
 When the Queen Regent\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 gives me a command\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 I carry it out without delay.

599
00:40:44.140 --> 00:40:47.340
Cersei must have\h\h\h
great trust in you

600
00:40:47.410 --> 00:40:51.050
  allowing you into her chamber
  during the hour of the wolf.\h

601
00:40:56.050 --> 00:40:58.350
 The Queen Regent has\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 a great many responsibilities.

602
00:40:58.420 --> 00:40:59.920
  She often works\h\h\h\h\h
  from dusk till dawn.

603
00:40:59.990 --> 00:41:04.230
She must be very glad\h\h
to have you helping her
from dusk till dawn.\h\h\h

604
00:41:05.800 --> 00:41:06.960
  Ah.

605
00:41:07.030 --> 00:41:08.330
   Lavender oil.

606
00:41:08.400 --> 00:41:10.700
  She always loved\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  lavender oil even as a girl.

607
00:41:10.770 --> 00:41:12.900
   I am a knight!

608
00:41:12.970 --> 00:41:15.070
   An anointed knight yes.

609
00:41:15.140 --> 00:41:17.510
Tell me\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
did Cersei have
you knighted\h\h\h

610
00:41:17.580 --> 00:41:19.880
 before or after she\h\h\h
 took you into her bed?

611
00:41:21.550 --> 00:41:24.150
  What? Nothing to say?

612
00:41:24.220 --> 00:41:25.780
   No more warnings
   for me ser?\h\h\h\h

613
00:41:25.850 --> 00:41:27.580
   You will withdraw\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
   these filthy accusations.

614
00:41:27.650 --> 00:41:29.450
  Have you ever\h\h\h\h
  given any thought

615
00:41:29.520 --> 00:41:31.250
   to what King Joffrey
   will have to say\h\h\h\h

616
00:41:31.320 --> 00:41:34.420
when he finds out\h\h
you've been bedding
his mother?\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

617
00:41:38.700 --> 00:41:40.030
   It's not my fault!

618
00:41:40.100 --> 00:41:42.930
 Did she take you\h\h
 against your will?

619
00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:44.770
   Can you not defend yourself
   knight?\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

620
00:41:44.840 --> 00:41:48.170
 Your own father Lord Tywin
 when I was named\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 the King's squire\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

621
00:41:48.240 --> 00:41:50.240
 he told me to obey
 her in everything.

622
00:41:50.310 --> 00:41:52.170
  Did he tell you\h\h
  to fuck her too?

623
00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:55.280
   I only meant I\h\h\h
   did as I was bid.

624
00:41:55.350 --> 00:41:57.050
 Hated every moment of it

625
00:41:57.120 --> 00:41:59.210
 is that what\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 you'll have me believe?

626
00:41:59.280 --> 00:42:01.220
 A high place in court
 a knighthood\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

627
00:42:01.290 --> 00:42:03.520
 my sister's legs spreading
 open for you at night.\h\h\h\h

628
00:42:03.590 --> 00:42:06.020
 Oh yes\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 it must have been terrible.

629
00:42:06.090 --> 00:42:08.060
 Wait here. His Grace\h\h\h
 will want to hear this.

630
00:42:08.130 --> 00:42:09.990
  Mercy! Mercy\h\h\h\h\h\h
  my lord! I beg you.

631
00:42:10.060 --> 00:42:12.160
Save it for Joffrey.\h\h\h
He loves a good grovel.

632
00:42:12.230 --> 00:42:14.630
 My lord it was\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 your sister's bidding
 the Queen.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

633
00:42:14.700 --> 00:42:16.400
   I'll leave the city
   at once I swear.\h\h

634
00:42:16.470 --> 00:42:17.970
   No I think not.

635
00:42:18.670 --> 00:42:19.670
 My lord?

636
00:42:20.340 --> 00:42:21.500
You heard me.

637
00:42:25.440 --> 00:42:28.680
  My father told you
  to obey my sister.
  Obey her.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

638
00:42:28.750 --> 00:42:31.410
Stay close to her side.
Keep her trust.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

639
00:42:31.480 --> 00:42:33.980
 Pleasure her\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 whenever she requires.

640
00:42:34.050 --> 00:42:38.520
 No one ever need know
 as long as you\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 keep faith with me.\h\h\h

641
00:42:40.760 --> 00:42:43.060
  I want to know\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  what Cersei is doing

642
00:42:43.130 --> 00:42:47.730
 where she goes who she sees\h
 what they talk of everything.

643
00:42:48.970 --> 00:42:50.130
  And you will tell me.

644
00:42:51.270 --> 00:42:53.200
 Yes my lord I will.

645
00:42:53.270 --> 00:42:54.740
 I swear it as you command.

646
00:42:58.010 --> 00:43:00.910
Oh rise rise.

647
00:43:00.980 --> 00:43:03.680
 Let us drink to\h\h\h
 our understanding.

648
00:43:03.750 --> 00:43:06.820
  Oh you don't have a cup.
  Oh well.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

649
00:43:06.880 --> 00:43:09.720
 Smile cousin. My sister
 is a beautiful woman\h\h\h

650
00:43:09.790 --> 00:43:11.290
 and it's all for\h\h\h\h\h\h
 the good of the realm.

651
00:43:11.360 --> 00:43:13.660
 Go back and tell her\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 that I beg her forgiveness

652
00:43:13.720 --> 00:43:15.790
that I want no more
conflict between us

653
00:43:15.860 --> 00:43:19.490
and that henceforth
I shall do nothing\h\h\h
without her consent.\h

654
00:43:19.560 --> 00:43:21.360
   But her demands?

655
00:43:21.430 --> 00:43:24.170
 Oh I'll give her Pycelle.

656
00:43:24.230 --> 00:43:26.200
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h You will?
\h
 Yes I'll release him\h\h\h\h
 in the morning.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

657
00:43:26.270 --> 00:43:28.040
 Cersei can keep him\h\h\h\h
 as a pet if she wants

658
00:43:28.110 --> 00:43:30.110
 but I will not have
 him on the Council.

659
00:43:30.170 --> 00:43:32.740
 I could swear\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 that I had not harmed\h\h\h\h\h
 a single hair on his head

660
00:43:32.810 --> 00:43:36.010
 but that would not\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 strictly speaking be true.

661
00:43:42.450 --> 00:43:43.850
(WOOD CREAKING)

662
00:43:47.130 --> 00:43:50.130
 MAN:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 Stay within one table length.

663
00:43:55.330 --> 00:43:56.700
 Your Grace.

664
00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:04.540
 Do your knucklebones
 bring you luck?\h\h\h\h\h

665
00:44:07.440 --> 00:44:10.780
 Well life's been good
 since you hacked\h\h\h\h\h\h
 them off Your Grace.\h

666
00:44:10.850 --> 00:44:12.950
  And it's four less\h\h\h
  fingernails to clean.

667
00:44:13.020 --> 00:44:14.950
Fewer.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
\h
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h Pardon?

668
00:44:16.290 --> 00:44:18.990
 Four fewer\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 fingernails to clean.

669
00:44:19.060 --> 00:44:22.260
 Never understood why\h
 you had to wear them.

670
00:44:22.330 --> 00:44:26.160
It reminds me of\h\h\h
where I come from\h\h
and where I am now.

671
00:44:26.230 --> 00:44:27.830
 It reminds me\h\h\h
 of your justice.

672
00:44:27.900 --> 00:44:30.570
It was an honest punishment
and you were good\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
with the cleaver.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

673
00:44:30.630 --> 00:44:32.930
 You were a hero
 and a smuggler.

674
00:44:34.670 --> 00:44:38.570
 A good act does\h\h\h\h\h\h
 not wash out the bad
 nor a bad the good.\h\h

675
00:44:40.080 --> 00:44:42.480
A lesson I've tried
to teach my son.\h\h\h

676
00:44:42.550 --> 00:44:43.580
 Does he listen?

677
00:44:43.650 --> 00:44:44.650
  To me?

678
00:44:44.720 --> 00:44:45.980
  Gods no.

679
00:44:47.580 --> 00:44:50.120
But if your red woman\h\h
told him to leap\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
from the crow's nest...

680
00:44:50.190 --> 00:44:51.720
  She has a name.

681
00:44:55.260 --> 00:44:57.990
 I trust you've not forgotten
 your smuggler's tricks.\h\h\h\h\h

682
00:45:00.560 --> 00:45:02.170
  I've lived within
  the law for 17...

683
00:45:02.230 --> 00:45:04.470
 I want you to be\h\h\h\h\h
 a smuggler this time.

684
00:45:05.540 --> 00:45:07.600
  Any shore any night.

685
00:45:07.670 --> 00:45:09.010
 What am I bringing ashore?

686
00:45:09.070 --> 00:45:10.570
 The red woman.

687
00:45:12.640 --> 00:45:16.310
 No one must know\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
 what you do and we'll not
 speak of this again.\h\h\h\h\h

688
00:45:16.380 --> 00:45:20.420
I am true to Your Grace
and always will be\h\h\h\h

689
00:45:20.480 --> 00:45:23.090
  but surely there are\h\h\h\h\h
  other ways cleaner ways.

690
00:45:23.150 --> 00:45:25.490
Cleaner ways don't
win wars.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

691
00:45:55.290 --> 00:45:57.490
  Are you afraid
  Onion Knight?\h\h

692
00:46:00.720 --> 00:46:05.630
   Someone once told me
   the night is dark\h\h\h
   and full of terrors.

693
00:46:05.700 --> 00:46:08.560
   You've carried\h\h\h\h\h
   more unpleasant\h\h\h\h
   cargo in your time.

694
00:46:12.540 --> 00:46:15.600
Are you a good man
Ser Davos Seaworth?

695
00:46:15.670 --> 00:46:19.610
 I'd say my parts\h\h\h
 are mixed my lady
 good and bad.\h\h\h\h\h\h

696
00:46:19.680 --> 00:46:23.880
   If half an onion\h\h\h\h
   is black with rot\h\h
   it's a rotten onion.

697
00:46:23.950 --> 00:46:26.280
   A man is good\h
   or he is evil.

698
00:46:26.350 --> 00:46:29.280
And which are you?\h\h\h\h\h
\h
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h  Oh good.

699
00:46:29.350 --> 00:46:34.360
 I'm a knight myself of sorts
 a champion of light and life.\h

700
00:46:35.830 --> 00:46:38.160
 Well that must be
 very nice for you.

701
00:46:54.480 --> 00:46:58.250
 Do you love your wife?
\h
 I do.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

702
00:46:58.320 --> 00:47:00.380
 Yet you have\h\h\h\h\h\h
 known other women.

703
00:47:00.450 --> 00:47:02.220
 Don't talk about my wife.

704
00:47:02.290 --> 00:47:04.950
   I'm not. I'm talking
   about other women.\h\h

705
00:47:06.620 --> 00:47:08.360
Like me Ser Davos.

706
00:47:13.100 --> 00:47:15.160
You want me.

707
00:47:15.230 --> 00:47:17.500
  You want to see\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h
  what's beneath this robe.

708
00:47:20.240 --> 00:47:21.700
And you will.

709
00:47:26.340 --> 00:47:28.680
 Strange that\h\h\h\h\h\h
 this Lord of Light

710
00:47:28.750 --> 00:47:31.050
 asks you to work
 in the shadows.\h

711
00:47:32.550 --> 00:47:35.720
Shadows cannot live\h\h\h\h
in the dark Ser Davos.

712
00:47:35.790 --> 00:47:40.520
They are servants of light
the children of fire.\h\h\h\h\h\h

713
00:47:40.590 --> 00:47:43.960
And the brighter the flame
the darker they are.\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

714
00:47:44.030 --> 00:47:46.560
 These weren't here before.\h
 They've barred the passage.

715
00:47:48.170 --> 00:47:50.400
 They can't bar
 our passage.\h\h

716
00:47:55.770 --> 00:47:57.540
  Gods protect us.

717
00:47:57.610 --> 00:48:01.180
  There's only one god
  Ser Davos\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h

718
00:48:01.250 --> 00:48:03.580
   and he only protects
   those who serve him.

719
00:48:03.650 --> 00:48:04.710
  (GASPS)

720
00:48:12.220 --> 00:48:13.260
   (LAUGHS)

721
00:48:13.320 --> 00:48:14.360
   (GASPS)

